{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-bundle-initial-conditions","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:bundle-initial-conditions","kind":"definition","title":"Bundle initial conditions","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hadron"],"tags":["bundle","initial-conditions","knot","categorical","configuration-space"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BundleInitialConditions","text":"bundle-initial-conditions.md","leanSource":"bundle-initial-conditions.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:bundle-initial-conditions\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}(V)</code> be the projective line, with a reference point in an affine chart. A <strong>bundle initial condition</strong> is a formal sum of localized hadrons and photons at base points,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{S}_0 = \\sum_{i \\in I} (p_i, H_i),</code></pre>\n<p>where each <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(p_i, H_i)</code> is a localized hadron or a photon, the index set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> may be infinite, and multiple constituents may share the same base point.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/measurement-observation/bundle-initial-conditions.md","heading":"Definition","number":"23.2.2","page":"b/def-bundle-initial-conditions","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BundleInitialConditions","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/measurement-observation/bundle-initial-conditions.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
